-- title:
--   Tame cyclic covers of the node xy=πⁿ are nodes
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, let $\pi \in W$ be irreducible, let $n > 0$ be invertible in $W$, and assume $W$ contains a primitive $n$-th root of unity. Write $R_0 = \mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\ W\ (\pi^{1\cdot n})$ for the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $W[[X_0,X_1]]$ by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - \pi^{1\cdot n}$ (the exponent is written $1 \cdot n$), and for $w \in W$ let $\mathrm{const}$ denote the class of the constant series $w$ in such a quotient. Let $B$ be a Noetherian local commutative domain that is integrally closed, equipped with an $R_0$-algebra structure which is module-finite and for which the scalar action is faithful; let $K_0$ be a fraction field of $R_0$ and $F$ a field which is simultaneously a $K_0$-algebra and an $R_0$-algebra compatibly, a $B$-algebra compatibly over $R_0$, and a fraction field of $B$. Assume $F/K_0$ is finite, Galois, with cyclic automorphism group, and $[F:K_0] = n$; assume that for every prime $\mathfrak p$ of $B$ whose contraction along $R_0 \to B$ has height $1$ the algebra $B$ is unramified over $R_0$ at $\mathfrak p$; and assume every $b \in B$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $B$ to the image in $B$ of $\mathrm{const}\ (\pi^{1\cdot n})\ w$ for some $w \in W$. Then there is a ring isomorphism $e : B \xrightarrow{\sim} W[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1 - \pi)$ with $e$ carrying the image in $B$ of $\mathrm{const}\ (\pi^{1\cdot n})\ w$ to $\mathrm{const}\ \pi\ w$ for every $w \in W$.
--
--   This is the Kummer-theoretic recognition step for tame cyclic covers of a node: a normal, module-finite, generically cyclic degree-$n$ cover of the crossing model of thickness $n$ which is unramified over all height-one primes and has constant residues is itself the crossing model of thickness one over the same coefficient ring. It feeds the description, by [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_uvCrossingModel_of_moduleFinite_of_isUnramifiedAt_of_isGalois`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_uvCrossingModel_of_moduleFinite_of_isUnramifiedAt_of_isGalois), of the completed local rings of the stable model at supersingular points, the case $n = p-1$ being the one used there.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_exists_ringEquiv_uvCrossingModel_of_isGalois_of_isCyclic_of_isUnramifiedAt_of_residue.lean

